{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.LinearChainBondFactorization","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.LinearChainBondFactorization","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Log.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.LinearChainBond.log_chainRatio_succ_neutron","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.LinearChainBond.log_chainRatio_succ_neutron","kind":"theorem","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/LinearChainBondFactorization.lean#L125-L131","doc":"Adding one neutron adds exactly `Real.log f_nn` to the log-ratio. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.LinearChainBond.chainRatio_neutron_slope_indep","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.LinearChainBond.chainRatio_neutron_slope_indep","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/LinearChainBondFactorization.lean#L109-L117","doc":"**Z-independence of the per-neutron multiplier** (division-free\ncross-multiplied form): the step `ratio(·, N) → ratio(·, N+1)` is the same\nfor every proton count. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.LinearChainBond.chainRatio_closed_form","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.LinearChainBond.chainRatio_closed_form","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/LinearChainBondFactorization.lean#L90-L107","doc":"**Closed form** (the audit's exact additive chain, multiplicatively):\n`ratio(Z, N) = f_pp^(Z−1) · f_pn · f_nn^(N−1)` for `Z, N ≥ 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.LinearChainBond.chainRatio_one_neutron","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.LinearChainBond.chainRatio_one_neutron","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/LinearChainBondFactorization.lean#L65-L88","doc":"Base of the tower: one neutron. The `Z` bonds are `Z − 1` pp's and the\nsingle pn interface: `ratio(Z, 1) = f_pp^(Z−1) · f_pn`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.LinearChainBond.chainRatio_succ_neutron","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.LinearChainBond.chainRatio_succ_neutron","kind":"theorem","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/LinearChainBondFactorization.lean#L48-L63","doc":"**Per-neutron multiplicativity** (the bean-2o66 lemma). For `Z, N ≥ 1`,\nadding one neutron appends exactly one `nn` bond: the trace ratio is\nmultiplied by `f_nn`, so it is exactly geometric in `N` — and the multiplier\ndoes not mention `Z`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.LinearChainBond.chainRatio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.LinearChainBond.chainRatio","kind":"def","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/LinearChainBondFactorization.lean#L42-L46","doc":"The chain trace ratio `tr_free / tr_atom` of the `(Z, N)` atom word in the\ndistinct-generator bond model: the product of the `A − 1 = Z + N − 1`\nper-bond factors. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.LinearChainBond.bondFactor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.LinearChainBond.bondFactor","kind":"def","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/LinearChainBondFactorization.lean#L36-L40","doc":"The factor carried by 0-indexed bond `i` (joining nucleons `i+1` and `i+2`\nin the `p^Z · n^N` order): `pp` while both endpoints are protons\n(`i + 2 ≤ Z`), `pn` at the single interface (`i + 1 = Z`), `nn` after. ","signatureChunk":0}]}